{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWordInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWordInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Relation"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.exists_Tw_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.exists_Tw_one","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L187-L192","doc":"The descended map sends the empty word — hence the identity of `W`, whenever `π`\nsends it there — to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.exists_Tw_of_braidEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.exists_Tw_of_braidEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L172-L185","doc":"**The `T_w` map exists as soon as the group half does.** If words with the same image\nin `W` are braid-equivalent, the word product descends to a well-defined function on `W`\nagreeing with it on every word.\n\nThis is a conditional theorem naming its hypothesis, which is the honest form of the\ndeferral — as opposed to a class that asserts the conclusion, or an instance that supplies\na placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_eq_of_braidEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_eq_of_braidEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L146-L151","doc":"Braid-equivalent words have the same product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_eq_of_braidMove","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_eq_of_braidMove","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L137-L144","doc":"**The algebra half of Matsumoto.** A braid move does not change the word product,\ndirectly from the defining braid relation of the Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.braidMove_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.braidMove_symm","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L132-L135","doc":"Braid moves are reversible: swapping the two indices runs the move backwards. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.BraidEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.BraidEquiv","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L126-L130","doc":"**Braid-equivalence**: the reflexive–transitive closure of `BraidMove`, i.e. any finite\nchain of braid moves in either direction is generated by the symmetric closure. Since the\n`BraidMove` constructor is symmetric in `(i, j)` — applying it with the pair swapped\nreverses the move — the reflexive–transitive closure is already an equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.BraidMove.move","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.BraidMove.move","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L123-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.BraidMove","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.BraidMove","kind":"inductive","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L120-L124","doc":"**One braid move**: inside a word, replace the alternating block `i j i ⋯` of length\n`M i j` by the alternating block `j i j ⋯` of length `M j i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_altWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_altWord","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L110-L118","doc":"**The word product of an alternating word is the alternating product.** This is the\nbridge between the list-level and algebra-level statements of the braid relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.length_altWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.length_altWord","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L104-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.altWord_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.altWord_succ","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L101-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.altWord_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.altWord_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.altWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.altWord","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L93-L97","doc":"The alternating word `i j i j ⋯` with `n` letters. Matches the recursion of\n`QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd`, so that the two agree under `heckeWord`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_append","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L83-L89","doc":"**Concatenation of words is multiplication.** The word product is a monoid map from the\nfree monoid on the generator index set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L80-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_cons","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L77-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord_nil","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidWord.heckeWord","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidWordInvariance.lean#L70-L73","doc":"The product `T_{i₁} ⋯ T_{i_k}` of the generators named by a word. ","signatureChunk":0}]}